{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Find research software"},"description":"Find research software for a task from the bio.tools registry (ELIXIR), check each tool's licence, verify the paper behind it (DOI, retractions, corrections), label whether it is still maintained, and give the install line. Describe the task (e.g. \"cluster single-cell RNA-seq data\") and optionally the file format the data is in (e.g. H5AD, FASTQ, VCF); tools that list that format as an input are favoured. Each result has a match level, a plain-language licence verdict, the paper and whether it checks out, a maintenance label (active, idle, stale, archived) read from the linked GitHub repository, and an install line built from a PyPI, Bioconda, Bioconductor, CRAN or GitHub link the registry lists. Every identifier and command comes from the registry's own records; nothing is generated. The `why` field lists the facts behind the match: explain the fit in your own words from those facts, and say plainly when no tool matched. Pass `keywords` with English words when the task is long or not in English. Licence verdicts come from registry and repository metadata and are not legal advice.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"citation_style":{"default":"apa","description":"Style for the ready-made paper citations.","enum":["apa","mla","chicago","harvard","vancouver","ieee","ama"],"type":"string"},"input_format":{"description":"The file format the data is in (e.g. \"H5AD\", \"FASTQ\", \"VCF\"). Tools that read it are favoured.","maxLength":30,"type":"string"},"intended_use":{"default":"publication","description":"What the software is for. `commercial` demotes anything its licence does not clear.","enum":["thesis","publication","commercial","teaching"],"type":"string"},"keywords":{"description":"English search ke